Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: loongarch/filter_lsx_intrinsics.c
Line: 237
Function: png_read_filter_row_avg3_lsx
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: __lsx_vldrepl_w(nxt, 0) reads 4 bytes from the current row without ensuring at least 4 bytes are available. With rowbytes == 3 (e.g., width 1, 3 bpp), this reads 1 byte beyond the row buffer.

Source context:
